F_FFAS<sector>A318 and transactions FOF_FFAF<sector>A318, quarterly, flat file fof2_en.zip; rows are the finest sectors that add up to all holders (sector 700), with a sector's figure minus its listed parts where they leave something out; figures before 2005 are on the 1993 SNA basis","note":"Every owner is a sector of the Bank of Japan's flow of funds, the Bank's own count of who holds all of it, in yen. Foreign investors are owners who live outside Japan. Net bought is the Bank's quarterly transactions; price and other changes is the change in holdings minus what was bought, which is the reconciliation the Bank publishes. The Bank changed its accounting basis in the first quarter of 2005, so a window that includes that quarter carries the change in price and other changes. Source: Bank of Japan. These are the certificates investors hold in investment trusts. The trusts in turn hold shares and bonds that appear in the other Japanese books, so this pool overlaps them: stock investment trusts alone held about an eighth of all listed Japanese shares in June 2026. The Investment Management Association of Japan's own count of the trusts' net assets at the end of June 2026 was 494.7 trillion yen, funds of funds counted twice; the Bank's figure here is 498.0 trillion, seven tenths of a percent higher."}